## 1. Purpose

The Elah Community License (ECL) is intended to support open development, community adoption, and commercial sustainability of the Elah video editing engine and related software.

This license allows developers and organizations to use, modify, and integrate the Software into their own applications while protecting the Software from unauthorized resale, rebranding, or competing hosted platforms.

---

## 2. Definitions

* **"Software"** means the source code, binaries, assets, examples, documentation, and related materials distributed under this license.
* **"Licensor"** means Elah and its contributors.
* **"You"** means any individual or legal entity using the Software.
* **"Derivative Work"** means any modified version, extension, adaptation, or enhancement of the Software.
* **"Hosted Service"** means a commercial product or platform where the Software itself is exposed as a primary service, editor, API, infrastructure layer, or SaaS offering to third parties over a network.

